Vita: marks between the main loop steps (twv_vita_loop_mark, platform/vita/gfx_vgl/
profile_hooks.cpp). The console session of 10 Nov left about 1.45 ms per game tick and 0.9 ms per frame of
the main loop outside every timer. A mark reads the clock once; the platform adds the time between
two marks to a receipt: the loop head (frame begin to the tick count), each tick input reads and
tail (camera commands, audio, commit), the presentation set-up, pass and end, and the loop tail.
Without the platform hook the marks do nothing. No game behaviour changes.

--- a/src/m_Do/m_Do_main.cpp
